  "details": "Hi Carlos Ratcliff Feature Request – Google Cardboard Headset Compatibility Dear VRChat Development Team, I am writing to respectfully submit a formal feature request for the integration of Google Cardboard headset compatibility into the VRChat application. As a dedicated user of your platform, I believe this enhancement would significantly broaden VRChat's accessibility and user base. Google Cardboard represents one of the most widely adopted and cost-effective entry points into virtual reality, enabling millions of users globally to experience VR through their existing smartphones. Currently, VRChat's platform support is limited to higher-end devices, which inadvertently excludes a substantial segment of potential users who lack access to premium hardware. I respectfully submit the following considerations in support of this request: I. Accessibility and Affordability Google Cardboard headsets are available at a fraction of the cost of devices such as the Meta Quest or Valve Index. Extending compatibility to this platform would make VRChat accessible to users across all socioeconomic backgrounds, in alignment with a commitment to inclusive design. II. Expanded Global Reach In numerous regions worldwide, budget-friendly VR solutions such as Google Cardboard serve as the primary means of accessing virtual reality experiences. Compatibility with this platform would position VRChat to engage a broader, more geographically diverse user community. III. Community Enrichment A more inclusive and diverse user base contributes positively to the culture and vitality of the VRChat community. New users from varied backgrounds bring creativity, perspective, and engagement that strengthen the platform as a whole. IV. Technical Viability Google Cardboard operates via standard smartphone gyroscope and accelerometer sensors. Implementation could be achieved through Google's Cardboard SDK or the widely supported WebXR Device API, making this a technically feasible and relatively low-barrier enhancement. I fully acknowledge the complexity of your development roadmap and the many competing priorities your team manages. However, I am confident that this feature would represent a meaningful investment in the long-term growth and accessibility of VRChat. I would welcome any opportunity to provide further input or clarification regarding this request. Thank you for your time and consideration. Respectfully submitted, Carlos Ratcliff",
